  "title": "How to install PHP in Windows 10? - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>PHP is a general-purpose scripting language geared towards web development. It is an open-source software (OSS), which is free to download and use. PHP stands for \"Hypertext Preprocessor\". PHP files are saved with an extension called .php. It supports many databases MySQL, Oracle, etc.</span></p><h2><b><strong>Installation of PHP on Windows</strong></b></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Follow the below steps to install PHP on Windows:</span></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> Visit </span><u><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic GFGEditorTheme__textUnderline\">https://www.php.net/downloads</em></i></u><span> website using any web browser and click on Downloads.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-1.png\" width=\"1100\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095205/1-660x355.png  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095205/1-768x413.png  768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095205/1-1024x550.png  1024w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095205/1.png, \"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2: </strong></b><span>Click on the Windows \"</span><b><strong>Downloads</strong></b><span>\" button.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-2.png\" width=\"1100\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095222/2-660x352.png  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095222/2-768x410.png  768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095222/2-1024x546.png  1024w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095222/2.png, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3:</strong></b><span> The new webpage has different options, choose the Thread safe version, and click on the zip button and Download it.</span></p></blockquote><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-3.jpg\" width=\"1050\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230607094930/php-(1).jpg 1050w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230607094930/php-(1)-100.jpg 100w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230607094930/php-(1)-200.jpg 200w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230607094930/php-(1)-300.jpg 300w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230607094930/php-(1)-660.jpg 660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230607094930/php-(1)-768.jpg 768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20230607094930/php-(1)-1024.jpg 1024w, \" loading=\"lazy\"><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 4: </strong></b><span>Now check for the zip file in downloads in your system and extract it.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-4.png\" width=\"1100\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075529/4-660x371.png  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075529/4-768x432.png  768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075529/4-1024x576.png  1024w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075529/4.png, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 5: </strong></b><span>After extracting, you get the extracted folder.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-5.PNG\" width=\"1100\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075711/5-660x354.PNG  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075711/5-768x412.PNG  768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075711/5-1024x549.PNG  1024w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075711/5.PNG, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 6:</strong></b><span> Now copy the extracted folder.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-6.png\" width=\"1100\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075801/6-660x371.png  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075801/6-768x432.png  768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075801/6-1024x576.png  1024w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075801/6.png, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 7: </strong></b><span>Now paste the copy folder in your windows drive in the Program files folder.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-7.png\" width=\"1100\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075923/7-660x371.png  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075923/7-768x432.png  768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075923/7-1024x576.png  1024w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221075923/7.png, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 8:</strong></b><span> Now the Permission Windows appears to paste the folder in program files then click on \"Continue\".</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-8.PNG\" width=\"1100\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080115/8-660x355.PNG  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080115/8-768x413.PNG  768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080115/8-1024x550.PNG  1024w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080115/8.PNG, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 9: </strong></b><span>Now after pasting the folder then copy the address of the folder in program files.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-9.png\" width=\"1100\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080306/9-660x371.png  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080306/9-768x432.png  768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080306/9-1024x576.png  1024w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080306/9.png, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 10:</strong></b><span> Now click on Start Menu and search \"Edit the system environment variables\" and open it.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-10.png\" width=\"1100\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080625/10-660x371.png  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080625/10-768x432.png  768w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080625/10-1024x576.png  1024w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221080625/10.png, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 11: </strong></b><span>After opening System, Variable New window appears, and click on \"Environment Variables...\"</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-11.PNG\" width=\"543\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095312/11.PNG, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 12:</strong></b><span> Now go to the \"System variables\"</span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\"> Path o</em></i><span>ption and double click on </span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">Path</em></i><span>.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-12.PNG\" width=\"700\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095323/12-596x660.PNG  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095323/12.PNG, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 13: </strong></b><span>Next screen will open and click on the \"New\" button.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-13.PNG\" width=\"600\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095337/13.PNG, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 14:</strong></b><span> After New &nbsp;Paste the address we copy from program files to new and click on </span><i><em class=\"GFGEditorTheme__textItalic\">Enter</em></i><span> button.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-14.PNG\" width=\"703\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221081400/14-599x660.PNG  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211221081400/14.PNG, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 15:</strong></b><span> Now Click on the </span><b><strong>OK </strong></b><span>button.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-15.PNG\" width=\"702\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095351/15-597x660.PNG  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095351/15.PNG, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 16:&nbsp;</strong></b><span> Click on the </span><b><strong>OK </strong></b><span>button.&nbsp;</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-16.PNG\" width=\"706\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095408/16-597x660.PNG  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095408/16.PNG, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 17: </strong></b><span>Click on </span><b><strong>OK</strong></b><span> for saving changes.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-17.PNG\" width=\"541\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20220101095422/17.PNG, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 18: </strong></b><span>Now your PHP is installed on your computer. You may check by going to the \"</span><b><strong>Start</strong></b><span>\" menu typing Command Prompt. Open it.</span></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-18.jpg\" width=\"451\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211228172858/startcmd.jpg, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 19: </strong></b><span>When the Command Prompt opens, type </span><b><strong>php -v</strong></b></p></blockquote><p><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-19.png\" width=\"643\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211228172432/phpv.png, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 20:</strong></b><span> Now enter the command prompt to show the version of PHP installed on your computer.</span></p></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"./images/web-dev-221-img-20.png\" width=\"660\" height=\"inherit\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211228171959/php81-660x243.png  660w, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20211228171959/php81.png, \" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Finally, You have successfully installed PHP on your Windows 10 system.</span></p></div>",
  "textContent": "PHP is a general-purpose scripting language geared towards web development. It is an open-source software (OSS), which is free to download and use. PHP stands for \"Hypertext Preprocessor\". PHP files are saved with an extension called .php. It supports many databases MySQL, Oracle, etc.Installation of PHP on WindowsFollow the below steps to install PHP on Windows:Step 1: Visit https://www.php.net/downloads website using any web browser and click on Downloads.Step 2: Click on the Windows \"Downloads\" button.Step 3: The new webpage has different options, choose the Thread safe version, and click on the zip button and Download it.Step 4: Now check for the zip file in downloads in your system and extract it.Step 5: After extracting, you get the extracted folder.Step 6: Now copy the extracted folder.Step 7: Now paste the copy folder in your windows drive in the Program files folder.Step 8: Now the Permission Windows appears to paste the folder in program files then click on \"Continue\".Step 9: Now after pasting the folder then copy the address of the folder in program files.Step 10: Now click on Start Menu and search \"Edit the system environment variables\" and open it.Step 11: After opening System, Variable New window appears, and click on \"Environment Variables...\"Step 12: Now go to the \"System variables\" Path option and double click on Path.Step 13: Next screen will open and click on the \"New\" button.Step 14: After New  Paste the address we copy from program files to new and click on Enter button.Step 15: Now Click on the OK button.Step 16:  Click on the OK button. Step 17: Click on OK for saving changes.Step 18: Now your PHP is installed on your computer. You may check by going to the \"Start\" menu typing Command Prompt. Open it.Step 19: When the Command Prompt opens, type php -vStep 20: Now enter the command prompt to show the version of PHP installed on your computer.Finally, You have successfully installed PHP on your Windows 10 system.",
  "url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/php/how-to-install-php-in-windows-10"
}
